  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the impulse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>J</mi></mfenced></math> on the gun is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is the mass,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math>&nbsp;is the initial velocity and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;is the final velocity of the bullet.</p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (1) to calculate the required impulse.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>J</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>600</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>",
